message: "If you use or build on this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Instruction-Free Dataflow Fabric: Deterministic Multi-Model Inference on a Configurable Spatial Dataflow Fabric for Real-Time Edge Systems"
authors:
  - family-names: Rout
    given-names: Kulamani
version: v0.1
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23884182
date-released: 2026-11-02
repository-code: "https://github.com/kulamani007/instruction-free-dataflow-fabric"
type: software
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - dataflow accelerator
  - spatial computing
  - edge AI
  - real-time systems
  - deterministic latency
abstract: >-
  A fixed hardware skeleton that any CNN within its range can be configured to
  become, running as a circuit with no instruction processor in the inference
  loop; a compiler produces configuration, routing, memory and a static
  schedule, so worst-case latency is known in advance even when several models
  share the chip.
